{"cantica":"purgatorio","cantoNumber":21,"title":"Canto XXI","totalDuration":351.92,"segments":[{"id":1,"speaker":"narrator","text":"The natural thirst that can never be satisfied\nexcept by the water for which\nthe Samaritan woman pleaded\ntormented me.","startTime":0,"endTime":7.44,"words":[{"word":"The","start":0.081,"end":0.241},{"word":"natural","start":0.241,"end":0.801},{"word":"thirst","start":0.801,"end":1.281},{"word":"that","start":1.281,"end":1.561},{"word":"can","start":1.561,"end":1.761},{"word":"never","start":1.761,"end":2.081},{"word":"be","start":2.081,"end":2.201},{"word":"satisfied","start":2.201,"end":2.961},{"word":"except","start":2.961,"end":3.441},{"word":"by","start":3.441,"end":3.601},{"word":"the","start":3.601,"end":3.761},{"word":"water","start":3.761,"end":4.161},{"word":"for","start":4.161,"end":4.361},{"word":"which","start":4.361,"end":4.521},{"word":"the","start":4.521,"end":4.641},{"word":"Samaritan","start":4.641,"end":5.281},{"word":"woman","start":5.281,"end":5.681},{"word":"pleaded","start":5.681,"end":6.241},{"word":"tormented","start":6.241,"end":6.961},{"word":"me.","start":6.961,"end":7.44}]},{"id":2,"speaker":"narrator","text":"The path was rough and steep, and urgency drove me forward\nbehind my guide as I pitied the souls receiving their righteous punishment.\nThen—just as Luke tells us Christ appeared\nto two disciples on the road from his empty tomb—\na spirit materialized behind us, gazing down\nat the prostrate multitude. We hadn't noticed him\nuntil he spoke: \"My brothers, may God grant you peace!\"\nWe spun around, and Virgil offered\nthe proper greeting in return.\nThe spirit began: \"May the true court of heaven\nseat you in peace among the blessed—\nthat same court that banishes me to eternal exile!\"","startTime":7.44,"endTime":44.72,"words":[{"word":"The","start":7.521,"end":7.841},{"word":"path","start":7.841,"end":8.081},{"word":"was","start":8.081,"end":8.521},{"word":"rough","start":8.521,"end":8.841},{"